{
  "_about": [
    "The census of the modern controls' default layout (design 1.9): of the 128 recorded winning routes, which levels have a shot that NO camera position the level's",
    "bounds allow can bring clear of a control's hit rectangle, so that the control would swallow a shot the route needs. The accepted list is `shapes`, per window shape.",
    "TWO ARRANGEMENTS of the walk arrows are recorded (planning step 186, the owner's decision of 2026-10-16), each under its own name in `arrangements`: `split` (walk_left in the",
    "bottom-left corner, walk_right in the bottom-right one: the arrangement that ships) and `grouped` (both at the bottom left, planning step 180's: kept as an alternative, asked for",
    "by `--controls modern,arrows=grouped`). The `grouped` block is the old golden's own content, key for key. Everything that does not depend on the arrangement (the inputs, the",
    "first design's pair as one rectangle, the classic discs, the three corner buttons) is at the top level.",
    "VALID ONLY FOR THE LAYOUT IN `valid_for`, in particular for hit.grow_px = 0 on every control (the owner's answer to Q0, 2026-10-15: desktop and touch both, growth 0 in the",
    "data). test_mp_census fails if controls.json differs from `valid_for` in any number, and fails if the levels this list names are not the levels it computes, in either",
    "direction. A changed growth (a thumb's, a later measured data change) means the census is RE-RUN and the list re-signed by the owner before the list is relied on again (CTL-13 made modern the default in planning step 198); it",
    "is never edited here to make the suite pass. The tables below it are the design's own arithmetic, kept as data so that the test has an oracle which is not the code it tests.",
    "Labels and counts only: no level bound, spawn point or tap is written here (those are the original's and live under out/)."
  ],
  "_source": [
    "DERIVED from the independent python model out/parity/program/CTL/CTL6b/work/arrows_model.py (places and hits for both arrangements, written from the design's section 1 and the",
    "owner's decision alone; the routes and the camera model are deadzone_census.py's) by out/parity/program/CTL/CTL6b/work/oracle_golden_ctl6b.py, at the exact window widths 256 x aspect.",
    "The `grouped` block was diffed against the previous golden (git show HEAD:tests/golden/controls_census.json): every key equal. docs/planning/2026-10-15-modern-controls.md",
    "section 1.9 and Appendix A name the headline numbers of the grouped arrangement; planning step 186 those of the split one."
  ],
